    "narrative": "With the 2026 season entering the home stretch, today\u2019s board is relatively thin due to league-wide off-days, forcing us to lean heavily on our two active starters to carry the offensive load. **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) edges out **Gleyber Torres** (67.46) as our strongest play. **Dylan Beavers** benefits significantly from a high-upside matchup against Yesavage; the park factor adjustment of +16% combined with his lead-off spot against a righty creates an elite efficiency profile. Meanwhile, **Gleyber Torres** is poised for a bounce-back day against Herz. Given Herz\u2019s atrocious 9.00 xERA, the +19% SP skill boost to **Gleyber Torres** is the primary driver here, as he looks to exploit a pitcher who has been struggling to limit hard contact throughout September. \n\nOur bench decisions are largely dictated by the schedule, as stalwarts like **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Bryce Harper**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Lawrence Butler** are all unavailable due to off-days. With the rest of our roster\u2014including speed-threats like **Justin Crawford** and **Masyn Winn**\u2014inactive today, our optimization strategy is effectively on autopilot. We are essentially betting the house on the top-of-the-order production from **Dylan Beavers** and **Gleyber Torres** to maintain our standing in the 5x5 Roto categories. We currently have no active weather concerns or lineup uncertainty for these two, so the primary risk remains the inherent volatility of a small sample size in a two-man start scenario. We are playing for maximum efficiency to protect our remaining games-played cap, keeping depth pieces like **Yainer Diaz**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Will Smith**, **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Luis Arraez**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **JJ Bleday**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Zack Gelof**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Braden Montgomery** safely sidelined until the full slate resumes.",
